<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="pre-raid-best-in-slot">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/achievement_dungeon_gloryofthehero.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Pre-Raid Best in Slot for Restoration Druids</span></h2>This is an example of the best-in-slot gear from all PvE sources available before entering any raids. Look at this as the set you'll chase if you have no interest in raiding. If you do, then try and collect Celestial tier pieces and big slots like Weapons to give yourself the fastest advantage possible. Valor items often require you to farm quite a bit of reputation and are only slightly more powerful than Celestial equivalents.<br/>
<br/>Haste breakpoints can make Druid gearing quite awkward before you have your best set. You can use sim tools such as QE Live to determine what to wear based on what you currently own.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<div class="markup-table-wrapper">
<table class="exclude-units grid">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="vertical-align: top; width: 100%; max-width: 100%;">
<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>This list is very heavy with World Boss loot since it's much higher level than anything else available outside of raid. For a version without, check out the Celestial tab further down the page.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<div class="exclude-units">
